  ;;
  ;; :forms -- the request forms of wire 35, told apart by an ASCII token (the
  ;; path precedes it, any content follows it), and which native host answers
  ;; each. Until 2026-09-25 this list lived only in the comments of amu
  ;; tools/kexe_loader.c. `:status :proposed` marks a form a host answers
  ;; before the kexe loader does (OWNER, S5). fsync, make-temp-dir and
  ;; stat-nofollow are no longer proposed: the loader answers them from the
  ;; same compiled decisions as the static image (superproject adr-2609251400
  ;; C3, 2026-09-25). amu refuses a kexe-loader program whose literals carry
  ;; the token of a form the loader does not answer, by name.
  ;; No token contains another, so a host that does not know a form cannot
  ;; take it for a different one.
  :fs/app-data
  {:source-operation fs/app-data :effect :host/fs-app-data
   :compiler-wire-id 35
   :kotoba.security/classification :confidential
   :forms
   {:read {:token nil :request "<path>" :answer "the file's bytes"
           :answered-by #{:kexe-loader :linux-static}}
    :write {:token "WRITE_SEP" :request "<path>WRITE_SEP<content>" :answer "the content"
